## Slot vocabulary ({{slot-count}} slots inherited or declared)

Code-Meta-Type memorials inherit `:mm/Memory` (and `meta-type`) with no class-specific slots — concrete instances are codebase memorials that reference this meta-type via `has-meta-type:`.

{{slot-table}}

## Opt-in default behavior

Per the opt-in discipline: code-meta-type instances are NOT included in default `mem search` results unless `--scope code` is passed.  Markdown-corpus search remains unchanged; consumers explicitly opt into code-substrate queries when needed.

This preserves portability — when the xref index is unavailable (no Clojure runtime, lint failure, fresh checkout), the markdown corpus still works.  Code-substrate queries fail gracefully.

## Composition with adjacent classes

- **`codebase`** — concrete codebase memorials declare `has-meta-type: <this code-meta-type entity>`
- **`library`** — library studies often cite their target's codebase memorial
- **`bug`** — bugs in registered codebases cite the codebase memorial via `affects:`

